fuxi: 0131 -- copy only the rows that changed

A boot screen is static except for one progress bar, but the compositor reports a
full-screen rectangle every present, so the copy path wrote 10.4 MB and cleaned 10.4 MB of
cache each time, ~40 times a second.

Each row is now compared against the destination first: unchanged rows cost a read and
nothing else, changed rows are copied and flushed on their own.  Worst case (everything
changes) it is the previous cost plus the compare; the normal case is a few kilobytes.

Flushing per row, not per rectangle, is also what makes this correct -- the panel scans by
DMA, so every written row has to reach DRAM.

Harness: applied=130 skipped=0.
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/FuxiFramebuffer.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/FuxiFramebuffer.cpp
@@ -676,20 +676,31 @@
 			src = 0;
 		}
 		if (src != 0 && bpe == 4) {
-			for (int32_t y = 0; y < h; y++) {
-				memcpy((void *)(fPixels + (uint64_t)(dy + y) * fRowBytes + (uint64_t)dx * 4),
-				    (const void *)(src + s->offset + (uint64_t)(sy + y) * s->bytesPerRow + (uint64_t)sx * 4),
-				    (size_t)w * 4);
-			}
 			/*
-			 * The panel scans this buffer with DMA, so the copy has to reach DRAM.
-			 * It used to stay in the CPU cache: every present ran, reported success,
-			 * and the display never changed (9000 swaps, a frozen screen, and a
-			 * framebuffer grab that differed by 21 pixels in 20 s).  The direct path
-			 * flushes for the same reason; this one did not.
+			 * Copy only the rows that actually changed.
+			 *
+			 * A boot screen is almost entirely static: one progress bar animates,
+			 * everything else is identical frame to frame, and the compositor still
+			 * reports a full-screen rectangle every time.  Copying it all costs
+			 * 10.4 MB of writes plus 10.4 MB of cache cleaning per present.  A row
+			 * compare costs reads only, and an unchanged row costs nothing more.
+			 *
+			 * Each changed row is flushed on its own: the panel scans by DMA, so an
+			 * unflushed write stays in the CPU cache and never reaches the screen.
 			 */
-			flush_dcache64((addr64_t)(fPixels + (uint64_t)dy * fRowBytes +
-			    (uint64_t)dx * 4), (unsigned)((uint64_t)h * fRowBytes), FALSE);
+			for (int32_t y = 0; y < h; y++) {
+				void *dst = (void *)(fPixels + (uint64_t)(dy + y) * fRowBytes +
+				    (uint64_t)dx * 4);
+				const void *row = (const void *)(src + s->offset +
+				    (uint64_t)(sy + y) * s->bytesPerRow + (uint64_t)sx * 4);
+
+				if (memcmp(dst, row, (size_t)w * 4) == 0) {
+					continue;
+				}
+				memcpy(dst, row, (size_t)w * 4);
+				flush_dcache64((addr64_t)dst, (unsigned)((size_t)w * 4), FALSE);
+			}
+		}
 		}
 		s->release();
 	}
